  "servo_reality_check": "The MJCF actuator is NOT the datasheet servo. Pollen's class chosen_actuator gives every leg joint forcerange +-0.96 N.m, while the repo's verified entry for the fitted servo (Dynamixel XL330-M288-T, out/verify/electronics_verify.json, ROBOTIS eManual cited there) gives stall 0.52 N.m at 5.0 V - the model is 1.846x stronger than the cited stall torque. The class also sets kv = 0 and the model carries NO joint velocity limit, so the step-response peak velocities below are what the MODEL can do, not what the servo can do. The XL330's no-load speed is not recorded anywhere in this repo: CANNOT DETERMINE, and it must be added before any of these peak velocities is quoted as a hardware capability.",
